    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="cf620225-34ec-534a-b91d-4504edae9169" activityNameId="b07b40bb-6b3b-57d9-8e3e-83a7eca3927a" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Electricity, hydropower, at small hydropower plant, in waterworks infrastructure</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Electricity, hydropower, at small hydropower plant, in waterworks infrastructure
Sources: Baumgartner &amp; Doka (1998), Konersmann &amp; Jean-Baptiste (2000).;
UUID: fbf86ff0-3e7e-318d-a66a-d3c364ac0631
This dataset describes the production of electricity from an average small hydropower plant. The plant itself is integrated in an already existing waterworks infrastructure such as e.g. drinking water supply or irrigation system. Furthermore, the infrastructure and the potential energy of the water are included. Information about the consumption of lubricating oil as well as the land transformation and occupation is missing.
Location: Central Europe but also valid for other continents.
Technology: Average small hydropower plant integrated in existing infrastructure (e.g. drinking water supply, irrigation system). The average efficiency is 0.8. Annual production volume: 1.16GWh/a.
Time period: undefined
Production volume: na
Sampling: literature 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_fbf86ff0-3e7e-318d-a66a-d3c364ac0631.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
